    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Using Proposition <a href="/tag/49A1CD" data-tag="49A1CD">6.2.2.5</a>, we can identify the equivalence classes of $(-1)$-truncated object $U \in \calP (\calC )_{/j(C)}$ with sieves $\calC ^{(0)}_{/C} \subseteq \calC _{/C}$. It is not difficult to see that $j( f_{\alpha })$ factors through $U$ if and only if $f_{\alpha } \in \calC ^{(0)}_{/C}$. Consequently, the $(-1)$-truncation of $\coprod _{\alpha \in A} j(C_{\alpha }) \rightarrow j(C)$ is associated to the <em>smallest</em> sieve on $\calC $ which contains each $f_{\alpha }$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
